  "tagline": "Go graph database inspired by Google's Knowledge Graph, dormant since its 2019 release.",
  "description": "Cayley is an open-source graph database written in Go, started at Google in 2014 and inspired by the storage behind Freebase and the Knowledge Graph. It stores RDF-style quads on pluggable backends (Bolt, LevelDB, PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, CockroachDB or memory) and queries them with Gizmo (a Gremlin-like JavaScript dialect), a GraphQL-inspired language and MQL. The last release, v0.7.7, shipped in October 2019 and the last commits date from mid-2024; the repo is not archived but effectively dormant. It remains a readable example of a quad store, but new projects should use a maintained engine.",
